-- comments
1:1 plain -- A `<` followed by a letter or `>`, after a token that cannot end an
2:1 plain -- operand, opens markup (frontend.md §9.3): after `=`, `(`, `[` and `,`,
3:1 plain -- `->` and `<|`. The tokens show each `markup_open`. Markup is lexed but not
4:1 plain -- yet parsed, so each expression is one not_implemented at its `<`: 7:5,
5:1 plain -- 11:8, 15:7 and 15:15, 19:11, 23:10.
